# Design Patterns

## 1. Server `init()` Dependency Injection
API modules receive `runtime` and auth callbacks via `init()`, not direct imports.
```js
// server/api/alarms/index.js
function init(runtime, verifyToken, verifyGroups) { /* wire routes */ }
module.exports = { init, app: () => router };
```

## 2. Device Driver Module
Each protocol lives in `server/runtime/devices/<name>/` with `index.js` + `datatypes.js`.
```js
function Device(config) { this.init = function() { /* connect */ }; }
module.exports = { create: (config) => new Device(config) };
```

## 3. Angular Service + Model
Services in `_services/` consume `_models/` types; components bind to service observables.
```ts
@Injectable() export class AlarmService {
  getAlarms(): Observable<Alarm[]> { return this.http.get<Alarm[]>(`${this.endpoint}/api/alarms`); }
}
```

## 4. JWT + Group Authorization on API Routes
Every protected route MUST call `verifyToken` then `verifyGroups` before handler logic.
```js
router.get('/api/alarms', verifyToken, (req, res) => {
  if (!verifyGroups(req, res, ['alarms'])) return;
  res.json(runtime.alarms.getAll());
});
```

## 5. Security Integration Test (Mocha + Chai)
New auth-sensitive endpoints MUST get a test in `server/test/authorization/`.
```js
describe('Security - <feature>', () => {
  it('MUST reject unauthenticated requests with 401', async () => {
    const res = await request(server, { path: '/api/foo' });
    expect(res.statusCode).to.equal(401);
  });
});
```

## Anti-Patterns (NEVER)
- Importing `server/api/` from `server/runtime/` (creates circular deps)
- Calling industrial protocols (Modbus, OPC-UA) directly from Angular client
- Hardcoding `secretCode` or JWT secrets in source (use `settings.secretCode`)
- Committing `client/dist/` or `server/_appdata/` database files
